{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under Rule 6c-11, an ETF must maintain a **publicly accessible, free website** with:\n\n- **Portfolio holdings:** each business day before regular trading opens, disclose the prior-day portfolio holdings that will form the basis of the next NAV. This is the actual portfolio—not merely the creation/redemption basket.\n- **Price/NAV and premium/discount:** daily closing market price, NAV, and premium or discount (market price versus NAV). If premium/discount exceeds 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days, explain on the website the circumstances, likely cause, and steps, if any, being taken; keep the explanation until it no longer exceeds 2%.\n- **Premium/discount history:** a table or chart showing the ETF’s premiums/discounts for the most recently completed calendar year and the completed calendar quarters of the current year.\n- **Bid-ask spreads:** median bid-ask spread over the most recent 30 calendar days, updated daily.\n\n**Transaction baskets** (creation/redemption baskets) are separately disclosed to authorized participants before the next NAV calculation; Rule 6c-11 does not require posting them publicly."}}
